.TH ELASTIC-SWAP 8 "OCTOBER 2026" "elastic-swap 0.2.0" elastic-swap
.\" disable french spacing
.ss 12 0
.SH NAME
elastic-swap \- Dynamic swap management for zram, zswap, and swap files.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B elastic-swap
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.RB [ \-V | \-\-version ]
.I start|status|autoconfig|prepare
.SH DESCRIPTION
elastic-swap is a daemon started by
.B elastic-swap.service
at boot. It runs a pool of
.B zram
devices that grows as compression saves RAM and shrinks when idle, or
.B zswap
in front of disk swap, and creates preallocated swap files when memory runs
short. The swap mode and its tuning come from
.BR elastic-swap.conf (5);
auto mode picks them from the hardware.
.SH COMMANDS
.IP start
Set up swap and keep managing it until SIGTERM. Run by the service unit.
Stopping the service ends the daemon but leaves its swap active, so no page
has to come back into RAM; the next start adopts that swap, and at shutdown
systemd deactivates it.
.IP status
Print the status of elastic-swap; modules being used and their statuses.
.IP autoconfig
Print the recommended configuration for the current system without applying it.
.IP prepare
Create the swap file directory (a NOCOW btrfs subvolume on btrfs, a plain
directory elsewhere). The service unit runs it as
.B ExecStartPre=+
so that it escapes the sandbox of the daemon itself. It does nothing in the
.B zram
and
.B disabled
modes.
.SH OPTIONS
.IP \-\-dry\-run
Show what would be done without mutating system state. No
.BR modprobe (8),
.BR swapon (8),
.BR swapoff (8),
or sysfs writes are performed. elastic-swap never edits
.BR fstab (5). Compatible with
.BR start .
Exits 0 on a successful plan.
.IP "\-h, \-\-help"
Print help and exit.
.IP "\-V, \-\-version"
Print version and exit.
